    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (75.13) and **Jacob Wilson** (72.17), both of whom benefit significantly from favorable matchups against Pfaadt and Bennett, respectively. **Kyle Tucker** remains our premier utility option, capitalizing on a weak SP_xERA of 4.54, while **Jacob Wilson** surges into the starting lineup due to a high-efficiency park factor (+7%) and a strong top-of-the-order positioning. **Andy Pages** (72.12) is another standout, with his score bolstered by a favorable matchup and a slow opposing delivery that increases his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of speed. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (68.95) and **Jackson Merrill** (65.93) maintain high floors thanks to optimal lineup slots and solid plate discipline, even against challenging arms like Nola and Lambert.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer was the exclusion of **Sam Antonacci** (43.59), who narrowly missed the final cut. While **Sam Antonacci** possesses the elite sprint speed we covet, the projection model favored the higher individual hitting efficiency scores of **Wade Meckler** and the rest of our starting outfield. Risk management remains a primary concern today, specifically regarding **Gunnar Henderson** (61.80) and **Heliot Ramos** (50.02); both face elite pitching in deGrom and Sale, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** sees his base projection suppressed by an 19% penalty due to the SP's skill level, yet he remains in the lineup because his platoon advantage and leadoff spot are too valuable to bench. We are also monitoring \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Liam Hicks**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Andy Pages**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Kyle Tucker**; any significant drop in their assumed batting order will necessitate a recalibration of our daily efficiency targets.",
